{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1436092,
  "courseSlug": "react-native-the-practical-guide",
  "courseTitle": "React Native - The Practical Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "31197606",
      "title": "Managing Screen Content with KeyboardAvoidingView",
      "lectureOrder": 85,
      "videoOrder": 82,
      "sourceHash": "4d5807c4f4338315c2f260c75bb38c82c81dd77cebac128059875f2f6d57ef1b",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 4.49,
          "en": "Now for the rest of this section,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.49,
          "end": 7.39,
          "en": "we will work ourselves through the different screens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.39,
          "end": 9.04,
          "en": "and make sure that they look good",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.04,
          "end": 11.79,
          "en": "on different sizes and orientations.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.79,
          "end": 12.623,
          "en": "But for the moment,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 12.623,
          "end": 15.66,
          "en": "I wanna stay on this starting screen here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 15.66,
          "end": 18.23,
          "en": "And here, we have a problem with the keyboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.23,
          "end": 19.52,
          "en": "Now on Android,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 19.52,
          "end": 22.97,
          "en": "we might get that full-size overlay keyboard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 22.97,
          "end": 27.92,
          "en": "which we can close ourselves, which looks and works okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 27.92,
          "end": 30.15,
          "en": "But on iOS, we have a problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.15,
          "end": 32.97,
          "en": "There, if I toggle this built-in keyboard,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.97,
          "end": 36.55,
          "en": "which our actual app users would be getting,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.55,
          "end": 39.97,
          "en": "we see that we can't close it, there is no button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.97,
          "end": 43.74,
          "en": "and tapping on the background doesn't do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.74,
          "end": 46.16,
          "en": "And I also can't get to the input anymore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 46.16,
          "end": 48.69,
          "en": "so I basically broke the app now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 48.69,
          "end": 51.383,
          "en": "And that, of course, is totally unacceptable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.28,
          "end": 53.755,
          "en": "The solution for this problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.755,
          "end": 57.19,
          "en": "is thankfully built into React Native, though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.19,
          "end": 61.15,
          "en": "We can use a specific component that helps us with that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.15,
          "end": 63.253,
          "en": "The KeyboardAvoidingView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.38,
          "end": 66.39,
          "en": "which in the StartGameScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 66.39,
          "end": 68.82300000000001,
          "en": "can be imported from React Native.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.74,
          "end": 73.19,
          "en": "This is a component which you can use in your JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.19,
          "end": 76.31,
          "en": "to wrap other content with it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 76.31,
          "end": 80.89,
          "en": "other content that involves or contains an input field,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.89,
          "end": 84.19,
          "en": "and whenever the keyboard that opens up that content",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.19,
          "end": 88.66,
          "en": "that holds your input element and other elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 88.66,
          "end": 92.68,
          "en": "can be moved up so that you can still access it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 92.68,
          "end": 94.60300000000001,
          "en": "even though the keyboard is open.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 95.83,
          "end": 97.42,
          "en": "For this, all you have to do",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 97.42,
          "end": 101.75999999999999,
          "en": "is wrap this view here in StartGameScreen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.75999999999999,
          "end": 104.08,
          "en": "with this KeyboardAvoidingView.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.08,
          "end": 107.493,
          "en": "You wrap this around your view here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 108.33,
          "end": 110.2,
          "en": "The View with rootContainer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 110.2,
          "end": 113.7,
          "en": "now is wrapped by the KeyboardAvoidingView.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.7,
          "end": 117.05,
          "en": "Now, since this will now be our rootView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 117.05,
          "end": 120.17,
          "en": "the top-most View in this component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 120.17,
          "end": 122.46,
          "en": "this would break our style.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.46,
          "end": 125.52,
          "en": "If we save this, everything would be broken.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 125.52,
          "end": 126.57300000000001,
          "en": "The reason for that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.57300000000001,
          "end": 130.13,
          "en": "that we no longer get as much space as we can,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 130.13,
          "end": 132.75,
          "en": "but we need to get as much space as we can",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 132.75,
          "end": 136.11,
          "en": "on this root element, for the rest of the elements",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 136.11,
          "end": 139.403,
          "en": "to get their appropriate slices and to look good.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.55,
          "end": 142.3,
          "en": "Now, we can add the style prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 142.3,
          "end": 144.01,
          "en": "to add a style that makes sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 144.01,
          "end": 146.25,
          "en": "that we take all the available space,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 146.25,
          "end": 149.56,
          "en": "and for this I already added a new style object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 149.56,
          "end": 151.84,
          "en": "in the StyleSheet, which I named screen,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 151.84,
          "end": 153.26,
          "en": "which sets flex to one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 153.26,
          "end": 154.653,
          "en": "That's all I do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 155.98,
          "end": 158.551,
          "en": "And this screen style object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 158.551,
          "end": 162.52,
          "en": "can now be added to this KeyboardAvoidingView",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 162.52,
          "end": 165.023,
          "en": "with styles screen like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 166.04,
          "end": 168.573,
          "en": "With that, it looks better again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 169.89,
          "end": 173.43,
          "en": "Now, if you tap in there, nothing changes though;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 173.43,
          "end": 175.75,
          "en": "it still is not accessible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 175.75,
          "end": 180.11,
          "en": "because you cannot also configure the KeyboardAvoidingView.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 180.11,
          "end": 183.57,
          "en": "You can add a behavior, which either wants height,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 183.57,
          "end": 186.33,
          "en": "padding, or position as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 186.33,
          "end": 188.72,
          "en": "Now, I do recommend that you play around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.72,
          "end": 191.91,
          "en": "with those values to see the differences.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 191.91,
          "end": 195.253,
          "en": "Very often, in my experience, position works best.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 196.55,
          "end": 198.12,
          "en": "Now, if we save that, however,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 198.12,
          "end": 200.28,
          "en": "we notice that everything is broken again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 200.28,
          "end": 205.12,
          "en": "because what position will do, is it will try to move this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 205.12,
          "end": 207.839,
          "en": "as you can see if you tap in there, that is working now,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 207.839,
          "end": 212.28300000000002,
          "en": "out of the way so that we can still see it whilst typing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.18,
          "end": 216.15,
          "en": "But for this to move effectively,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 216.15,
          "end": 218.824,
          "en": "this needs to be in a scrollable container,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 218.824,
          "end": 221.32999999999998,
          "en": "which at the moment isn't.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 221.32999999999998,
          "end": 225.07,
          "en": "Therefore, to make position work great in this case here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 225.07,
          "end": 229.57999999999998,
          "en": "we should wrap the KeyboardAvoidingView, with a scroll view.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.57999999999998,
          "end": 232.15,
          "en": "Because we learned before that we can use a scroll view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 232.15,
          "end": 234.1,
          "en": "to add scrolling.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 234.1,
          "end": 235.96,
          "en": "We don't want flat list here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 235.96,
          "end": 238.12,
          "en": "because we don't have a dynamic list",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 238.12,
          "end": 240.98,
          "en": "with possibly an infinite amount of items,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 240.98,
          "end": 243.81,
          "en": "instead we have a clearly defined user interface,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 243.81,
          "end": 247.97,
          "en": "which should be scrollable in case we run out of space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 247.97,
          "end": 250.37,
          "en": "Therefore, we simply wrap ScrollView,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 250.37,
          "end": 253.223,
          "en": "around the KeyboardAvoidingView, like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 254.37,
          "end": 257.86,
          "en": "and on the scroll view, we should also add the style again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 257.86,
          "end": 259.64,
          "en": "and set this to styles screen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 259.64,
          "end": 261.24,
          "en": "to make sure that the scroll view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 261.24,
          "end": 263.88,
          "en": "occupies all the space it can get,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 263.88,
          "end": 267.12,
          "en": "because screen sets flex to one,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 267.12,
          "end": 269.6,
          "en": "so that we still get all the space we can get here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.6,
          "end": 272.29,
          "en": "and then here, and then all our other styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.29,
          "end": 275.49,
          "en": "can style themselves and lay themselves out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 275.49,
          "end": 277.693,
          "en": "based on that available space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 278.89,
          "end": 280.7,
          "en": "Now with that scroll view",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 280.7,
          "end": 284.15999999999997,
          "en": "wrapped around KeyboardAvoidingView if you save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 284.15999999999997,
          "end": 285.74,
          "en": "this looks good again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 285.74,
          "end": 289.32,
          "en": "and now you see this moves up as I start typing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 289.32,
          "end": 290.40999999999997,
          "en": "And I can scroll this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 290.40999999999997,
          "end": 292.85,
          "en": "to reach the different parts of this UI.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 293.85,
          "end": 296.85,
          "en": "Here on Android, we don't really see this, but that's okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 296.85,
          "end": 299.573,
          "en": "because we just needed it here on iOS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 300.89,
          "end": 304.14,
          "en": "Now with that, we can also tap somewhere else",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 304.14,
          "end": 305.87,
          "en": "to close this keyboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 305.87,
          "end": 309.203,
          "en": "That's a nice side effect of KeyboardAvoidingView.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 310.309,
          "end": 314.469,
          "en": "If you now tap this card here, the keyboard closes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 314.469,
          "end": 317.25,
          "en": "Now, if I tap here, it does not really close,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 317.25,
          "end": 321.47,
          "en": "at least not always, but we do have this main area covered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 321.47,
          "end": 322.73,
          "en": "and therefore we now of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 322.73,
          "end": 326.07,
          "en": "allow our users to always reach all these buttons,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 326.07,
          "end": 328.623,
          "en": "and they can also close the keyboard.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 329.69,
          "end": 332.32,
          "en": "So that's the KeyboardAvoidingView in action,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 332.32,
          "end": 334.72,
          "en": "which is another super important component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 334.72,
          "end": 336.56,
          "en": "exposed by React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 336.56,
          "end": 339.37,
          "en": "has nothing to do with expo as you see,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 339.37,
          "end": 341.58,
          "en": "but instead it's built into React Native,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 341.58,
          "end": 344.74,
          "en": "and it can help a lot with building accessible",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 344.74,
          "end": 347.493,
          "en": "and usable user input areas.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
